>> title: Panang Curry
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, coconut, thai, peanuts, curry
>> counters: Thai Kitchen, One Pot
>> aka: gaeng panang, phanaeng, penang curry, panang neua, panang beef, panang curry beef
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min

>> step: crack the cream 5 min
Fry @coconut cream{1%cup}(240 mL) in a #wok{} over medium heat for ~fry{5%min}, until it splits and beads its own oil.

>> step: fry the paste 3 min
Fry @panang curry paste{1/3%cup}(80 g) into @&(~1)cracked cream{} for ~fry{3%min}, pressing it flat against the pan.

>> step: simmer 10 min
Simmer @beef sirloin{1%lb}(450 g; sliced thin across the grain) and @coconut milk{1%cup}(240 mL) with @&(~1)fried paste{} for ~simmer{10%min}.

>> step: reduce 8 min until it coats
Reduce @&(~1)curry{} with @fish sauce{2%Tbs}, @palm sugar{1%Tbs} and @roasted peanuts{2%Tbs}(ground fine) for ~simmer{8%min}, until it barely pours and coats the back of a spoon.

>> step: scatter over
Scatter @makrut lime leaves{4}(rolled and cut into hairs) and @red spur chile{1}(slivered) over @&(~1)curry{}.
